---
import '../../styles/kit.css';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { href, pageMeta } from '../../lib/site';
import { docsArticle, docsBreadcrumbs } from '../../lib/jsonld';
const h1 = "Contributing";
---

<Page path="/docs/contributing" ogType="article" jsonLd={[docsArticle(h1, pageMeta('/docs/contributing').description, '/docs/contributing'), docsBreadcrumbs(h1, '/docs/contributing')]}>
	<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	    <div class="bd first"><div class="wrap"><h1 class="t60">Contributing</h1></div></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="k0" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="k0" class="t28">Ways to help</h2></div>
	<ul><li><strong>Run it and tell us.</strong> Nobody outside the project has run it on their own app yet. Your honest reaction is the most useful thing you can give us.</li><li><strong>Review it.</strong> If you’re an accessibility specialist, label a page and tell us where the tool is wrong.</li><li><strong>Report a finding that looks wrong.</strong> Use the &ldquo;A finding looks wrong&rdquo; template on GitHub. It helps most when you include the evidence line.</li><li><strong>Change the code.</strong> Most of the code is plain TypeScript that runs anywhere.</li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="k1" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="k1" class="t28">Before you change code</h2></div>
	<CodeBlock label={"Run the checks"} code={"pnpm install\npnpm test\npnpm run lint\npnpm run typecheck"} /><p>If those three pass, you can open a pull request for the rules, the judge, the command line and the report. They need no Windows machine. Changes to the capture part need a Windows machine running NVDA.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="k2" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="k2" class="t28">Licence</h2></div>
	<p>a11ign is licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later. Anyone who runs a modified version as a service has to share their changes. Questions about running it in CI are answered in the <a class="lnk2" href="https://github.com/a11ign/a11ign/blob/main/docs/licence-faq.md">licence FAQ</a>, which isn’t legal advice.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="k3" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="k3" class="t28">Getting help</h2></div>
	<p>This is a small project, so there is no promised response time. Open an issue on GitHub, or see <a class="lnk2" href={href('/contact')}>Contact and support</a>.</p>
	    </section></div>
	  </main>
</Page>

